From 58cd1a13fb2482eae14962f758aac9e2d349936e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nieyin345 <nieyin0703@outlook.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 23:57:06 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat(slides): reshell the chrome in Mcode's design tokens

Third batch of O6. Same 54 shared chrome token values as Docs (0014), HTML
(0016), Markdown (0017) and PDF (0018).

The gate matters more here than anywhere else: Slides' preload exposes
`desktop` as well as `slidesApi` (src/preload/index.ts:499, the attachment
API), so copying the Docs guard `if (window.desktop)` would fire in standalone
runs too - which is exactly what we measured happening to Docs. The gate is
the UA product token instead.

Slides carries 138 app-private tokens, and they are almost all content or
document semantics rather than chrome: --slides-paper, --slides-show-* (the
presenter's fixed black-on-white show), --slides-anim-* (PowerPoint's
entrance/emphasis/exit/path colour coding), --slides-crop-* with the guides
and grid, --slides-reading-* (fixed dark), --slides-laser-*. None are touched,
per the rule the PDF batch settled: the shell swap replaces shared tokens
only. App-private chrome (--slides-statusbar-bg, --slides-rail-bg,
--slides-focus-ring, --slides-shadow-menu) also stays put, because a per-app
override would split one menu into six greys.

canvas-colors.ts is left alone too: it holds three redact-frame values and is
drawing a document mark, not chrome.

o6-reshell-slides-smoke: 39/39 in real Electron, four modes (hosted/standalone
x light/dark), with the same two premises as the other suites (dark actually
reached the page; light != dark). Mutations: gate removed 11 red across the
standalone and dark-standalone groups, --surface reverted 1 red, --chrome-bg
reverted 1 red (independent of the previous one, as in PDF), import removed
12 red. No fixture is needed: standalone Slides opens a blank deck itself.
